/**
 * NewTabHint — the visually hidden «(открывается в новой вкладке)» that every
 * link leaving this site appends to its own accessible name (WCAG 3.2.5,
 * Issue #37).
 *
 * A component rather than a copied `<span class="ob-sr-only">` because the
 * string is the ASSERTION: `tests/e2e/interaction.spec.ts` sweeps every route
 * for it, and five hand-written copies are five chances for one of them to
 * drift a word and go quietly unannounced while the sweep still passes on the
 * other four.
 *
 * It is a SUFFIX, so it renders as the last child inside the anchor and opens
 * with a space: the accessible name is the concatenation of the link's text
 * nodes, and without the leading space «Программа конгресса» и «(открывается…)»
 * arrive as one word.
 *
 * Deliberately NOT an `aria-label` on the anchor: a label REPLACES the visible
 * text, which costs speech-input users the ability to say what they see
 * (WCAG 2.5.3) — the very trade-off VideoCard's header already refuses.
 *
 * Only where the `target` actually is. `PartnerTier` links МОО «ОРТО» to
 * `https://orthobio.ru/` — an absolute URL to THIS origin, which opens no tab —
 * so callers gate this on the same condition that writes the attribute, never
 * on «the href looks external».
 */
---

<span class="ob-sr-only"> (открывается в новой вкладке)</span>
